TASK-194 follow-up runtime harness (review fixes F2, F3, F6): Debug build, data
dir DetourVerify1941, 2026-10-27, macOS 26.7, light and dark. Temporary code,
never committed to Detour/. Gated on DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR; DETOUR_VERIFY_APPEARANCE
light or dark; DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT the fixture server's port;
DETOUR_VERIFY_SERVER_LOG its request log (Host, path, Referer);
DETOUR_VERIFY_DOWNLOADS a scratch folder (never ~/Downloads). Input after 12 s
of HID idle; captures by window number (screencapture -l) only.

Environment quirk met here: another app was active and cooperative activation
refused NSApp.activate, so the quarantine windows opened behind it, occluded,
and WebKit painted nothing. The harness orders the window in front with
orderFrontRegardless() (no activation). Setting window.level = .floating from
the harness Task trapped in AppKit (-[NSWMWindowCoordinator
performTransactionUsingBlock:], SIGTRAP), so it is not used. In an inactive
app's window a posted plain click is an activation click the page never sees;
a Cmd-click goes through. Plain clicks are therefore handed to the web view
(webView.mouseDown/mouseUp with real NSEvents) while the app is inactive.

